          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: Two witnesses report seeing, on July 31, 1994 at approximately 1:15 a.m., just above the hills east of Marseille, a red half-sphere about twice the size of the moon turning yellow as it shrunk. The witnesses witnessed the phenomenon disappear into a thin ray of light. The witnesses could not explain what they saw. This case was classified \"C\" due to a lack of information. In July 2012, a recreation at the same location and time will be conducted as part of a possible saros cycle (see explanations in the investigation report). Following a highly convincing recreation 18 years later, the GEIPAN reclassifies this case as \"A\": misidentification with the Moon at its rising.",
